# Test Immutability

Existing tests in `JobMatchTests/` are a regression contract. When implementing new logic, do not automatically change old tests to make CI green again.

## Never do automatically

When new logic breaks an existing test:

- Remove or comment out assertions
- Weaken expectations (`#expect(true)`, flip booleans, drop mock call checks)
- Rewrite the test scenario to match the new implementation without user approval

## What to do instead

1. **Default** — fix production code in `MatchFlow/` so the old test passes (preserve backward compatibility).
2. If behavior **intentionally** changes — stop and ask the user whether to update the test. Do not edit the old test without explicit approval.
3. **Adding new tests** for new logic is encouraged — add them alongside old tests, not instead of them.

## Examples

```swift
// ❌ BAD — old test failed after new logic, agent "fixed" the test
// AuthViewModelTests: #expect(viewModel.isAuthenticated) — removed or weakened

// ❌ BAD — updated expectation without asking the user
// was: #expect(mockService.signInCalled)
// now: #expect(!mockService.signInCalled)

// ✅ GOOD — old test failed → fix production, contract preserved
// new logic must not break existing signIn() scenarios

// ✅ GOOD — behavior really changes → ask the user first
// "signUp no longer logs in immediately — update AuthViewModelTests?"

// ✅ GOOD — added new tests for new logic, left old tests untouched
// JobDetailViewModelTests: +3 notes tests, existing loadJob tests unchanged
```

## Exceptions

- User **explicitly** asks to change or delete a specific old test.
- User **explicitly** confirms a contract change — then update test and code together, deliberately.
- Obvious bug in the test itself (typo, wrong mock setup) — fix without changing the behavior under test.

## Allowed

- New tests and mocks for new logic.
- Refactoring test infrastructure (fixtures, helpers) when assertions and scenarios stay the same.
- Editing old tests **after an explicit user request**.

## Relevant test files

Do not auto-edit these when adding new features:

- `JobMatchTests/Unit/ViewModels/AuthViewModelTests.swift`
- `JobMatchTests/Unit/ViewModels/JobDetailViewModelTests.swift`
- `JobMatchTests/Unit/ViewModels/JobsViewModelTests.swift`
- `JobMatchTests/Unit/ViewModels/DashboardViewModelTests.swift`
- `JobMatchTests/Unit/Services/AIServiceTests.swift`
